Overview:
We are looking for a Test Leader to join the Test Centre of a leading international insurance and financial services group, supporting testing services for its French operations. The role contributes to the Test Strategy, Master Test Plan and test design, and ensures the execution of test campaigns, the follow-up of test analysts and reporting to project stakeholders. You will report directly to the Test Centre Team Leader, working in Agile projects based in Lisbon and you will help ensure the functional quality of delivered increments and features.
What will you do?

• Contribute to the Test Strategy, Master Test Plan and test design activities;

• Contribute to the design of Business Analyst tests within projects, respecting project deliverables and the standards in place;

• Input test subjects into the dedicated testing tools according to defined standards;

• Ensure the elaboration, validation and communication of all testing deliverables within scope;

• Contribute to the implementation and execution of test campaigns, including their updates;

• Execute tests within the assigned scope of responsibility and record the results in the dedicated testing tools;

• Guarantee the correct prioritisation of tests and contribute to the organisation of Business Analyst knowledge;

• Follow up the work of test analysts and report to project stakeholders;

• Ensure the functional quality of increments and delivered features;

• Ensure the testability of Backlog items and features to be delivered;

• Provide the information required for Go/No Go decisions;

• Identify, register, prioritise and validate the correction of project anomalies;

• Report risks regarding project quality or delivery timelines;

• Provide regular feedback to the Test Manager and management regarding project progress;

• Create test reports to communicate with project stakeholders;

• Manage project committees related to test progress and defect follow-up;

• Contribute to the preparation of final reports and testing procedures;

• Contribute to the technical and methodological excellence of testing activities.

What are we looking for?

• Degree in Informatics, Computer Science or related areas;

• Minimum 5 years of experience in testing activities;

• Experience in the environment of the service: 0 to 2 years;

• Knowledge of test methodology principles and vocabulary (ISTQB);

• Experience creating Test Strategies and Test Schedules;

• Experience managing one or more software testers;

• Experience working within Agile environments;

• Knowledge of Octane, JIRA and Confluence;

• Knowledge of API testing;

• Knowledge of SQL language;

• Experience in risk identification, management and follow-up;

• Experience testing applications related to Life Insurance or Banking products (desirable);

• Experience with applications such as ORION, HERA, Wynsure and GLIS is considered an advantage;

• Coordination and motivation skills;

• Systematic, critical and logical thinking, with good summarisation capabilities;

• Strong commitment and sense of accountability;

• Pedagogical mindset and knowledge-sharing capability;

• Customer satisfaction orientation and ability to deliver high-quality results;

• Ability to manage stress and conflicts;

• Good listening and questioning skills;

• Good learning capabilities and adaptability to changes and evolving environments;

• Ability to plan work ahead and prioritise workload;

• Ability to travel outside Portugal;

• Willingness and ability to work outside normal office hours in exceptional circumstances;

• Fluent in French (mandatory);

• Professional level of English.

What can you expect from us?

• A permanent job contract for a long term project;

• Tech equipment + SIM Card + personal smartphone;

• Health and Life Insurance;

• Social events and team buildings;

• The commitment of letting you grow with us, and be rewarded accordingly;

• A dynamic and young team that will be always there to support y

Volunteer Program at PE Insights

Nordic's Largest PE Conference. Stockholm, November 24th &amp; 25th 2027

&nbsp;

Ready to take a major leap towards private equity, M&amp;A, banking or consulting? This is your chance to get a view behind the scenes of the world’s largest private equity community and be part of the volunteer team shaping the future of finance.

Challenge yourself to go outside your comfort zone with likeminded individuals who for two days will be your partners in the trenches facilitating the room of top-of-the pyramid PE professionals.

&nbsp;

Why Private Equity Insights

Private Equity Insights is the world’s largest Private Equity community with 1m PE professionals, delivering impact through 12 global PE conferences with thousands of the most world’s best investors and operators such as Blackstone, BlackRock, Apollo, Carlyle, CVC, KKR, and many more.&nbsp;

Private Equity Insights is part of United Media (https://www.united-media.com/) which focuses on building large-scale industry media and conferences products in sectors such as insurance, finance, retail, etc. As of today, we have organically launched 5 media companies and exited 1.&nbsp;

&nbsp;

What we offer you

You’ll be supporting the Private Equity Insights team in delivering the conference for sharp insights and inspiration, and outstanding network opportunities for the PE professionals we serve. Among other things the opportunity offer:

• Peer network: you join a select group of ambitious volunteers who will keep crossing your path for the next 40 years working in the industry.

• Insider knowledge. Where the day allows, you can sit in on panels, the same ones attendees come to hear. In fact, we encourage you to do so.

• Confidence under pressure: after two demanding conference days, high-stakes moments at work will feel easier.

• Master persuasion: learn to influence high-caliber professionals to deliver win-win results.&nbsp;

• A certificate to show on your CV and LinkedIn that you volunteered at Private Equity Insights.&nbsp;

• Fuel: food and refreshments on both days.

• Global programme: The long term opportunity to lead teams and become the person who shows the way for others, or even join Private Equity Insights full time.&nbsp;

&nbsp;

Your responsibilities

This is hands-on, operational work focusing on making the conference run. The work changes hour by hour, and you are expected to step in and help wherever the conference needs you.

&nbsp;

What the future hold for you with PE Insights&nbsp;

Whether you are with us for 1 conference or 10+, we believe this lays the foundation for a very successful career.&nbsp;

Exceptional volunteers have in the past been offered roles at Private Equity Insights, such as Investor Relations or Entrepreneur in Residence.

Others have gone on to join firms such as McKinsey, BCG, JP Morgan, Deutsche Bank, Ardian and Verdane.

&nbsp;

What we expect from you

We are looking for final-year undergraduates, master's students and early-career professionals with an interest in private equity, M&amp;A, banking, consulting or conferences. We expect you to:

• Have a relentless drive to become the very best at what you do

• Bring outstanding energy and a positive mindset from the first hour to the last

• Set aside 2 full days for the conference + online training leading up to

• Be curious to learn from top private equity professionals

• Stand out as the person others want beside them on a hard day

• Speak English at a professional level. Spanish is a plus

&nbsp;

This is an unpaid role. Applicants from outside Stockholm are welcome. You fully arrange your own travel and accommodation.&nbsp;

We review every application and invite shortlisted candidates to a short call. If you hold yourself to the standard described here, apply.
